" "answer-24a596ab-d572-5e03-98bd-b3bb211503d5" "answer-ec9b6b5f-92a6-5d44-819f-78e0d940c7e8" "answer-201f8e83-02c6-52d6-ba76-7acebff7db1b" "answer-df35242b-e6b7-5c1b-8b7a-4d5447cbd25f"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-eb813e12-ffc7-57a7-9a3b-bdb9d45f4fd1" :answer/id #uuid "eb813e12-ffc7-57a7-9a3b-bdb9d45f4fd1" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "sup(D)=4\\in D" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-24a596ab-d572-5e03-98bd-b3bb211503d5" :answer/id #uuid "24a596ab-d572-5e03-98bd-b3bb211503d5" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "sup(D)=4\\notin D" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-ec9b6b5f-92a6-5d44-819f-78e0d940c7e8" :answer/id #uuid "ec9b6b5f-92a6-5d44-819f-78e0d940c7e8" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "sup(D)=\\sqrt{3}\\in D" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-201f8e83-02c6-52d6-ba76-7acebff7db1b" :answer/id #uuid "201f8e83-02c6-52d6-ba76-7acebff7db1b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "sup(D)=\\sqrt{3}\\notin D" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-df35242b-e6b7-5c1b-8b7a-4d5447cbd25f" :answer/id #uuid "df35242b-e6b7-5c1b-8b7a-4d5447cbd25f" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$sup(D)$ does not exist" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-402a4d55-ba8d-55eb-b6d0-1bc9813966c1" :question/id #uuid "402a4d55-ba8d-55eb-b6d0-1bc9813966c1" :question/math-academy-id "q-253134" :question/problem "Consider the following set.\n\n$$\nA=\\{(-1)^{n}\\cdot \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{n+1}}\\,:\\,n\\in N\\}\n$$\n\nFor this set, we have that {{field-1}}." :question/worked-solution "The supremum of $A$ is the smallest upper bound of $A.$\n\nTo find the supremum of this set, we must find the set containing **all** upper bounds of $A$ (i.e., the set of upper bounds) and take the minimum of this set.\n\nThe elements of $A$ are the terms of the sequence ${a}_{n},$ given by\n\n$$\n{a}_{n}=(-1)^{n}\\cdot \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{n+1}},\\,n\\in N=\\{1,2,3,4,…\\}.\n$$\n\nLet's draw some points of our sequence on the real line:\n\n![](images/69/690c0466ffac72597e9378539d1540d6baaa49c7cbe77bee8cc83ab00f065635.png)\n\nWe see that ${a}_{n}$ is an oscillating sequence converging to $0.$ The maximum of $A$ is \n\n$$\nmax(A)={a}_{2}=(-1)^{2}\\cdot \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2+1}}=\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{3}}.\n$$\n\nSo, in our case, we have that\n\n- any number $x\\ge {a}_{2}$ is an upper bound of $A,$\n\n- any number $x<{a}_{2}$ cannot be an upper bound because ${a}_{2},$ an element of $A,$ is greater than $x.$\n\nTherefore, $[\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{3}},\\infty )$ is the set of upper bounds of $A,$ and \n\n$$\nsup(A)=min[\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{3}},\\infty )=\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{3}}.\n$$\n\nNotice that $\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{3}}$ is the maximum of $A.$ Therefore, we conclude that\n\n$$\nsup(A)=\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{3}}\\in A.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-756d9f31-195b-5f29-8f95-74ae53b26047"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-756d9f31-195b-5f29-8f95-74ae53b26047" :answer-field/id #uuid "756d9f31-195b-5f29-8f95-74ae53b26047" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/select :answer-field/correct "answer-66c0e3c3-432e-504d-94dc-f89ea3bb6e76" :answer-field/choices ["answer-31543bec-7415-5c0a-b5bd-5fe9b03eaa24" "answer-fc17b842-d919-52cc-a3ae-905dd3045738" "answer-66c0e3c3-432e-504d-94dc-f89ea3bb6e76" "answer-7d275fd5-7007-526a-9ff9-feaa35579085" "answer-df2b4c83-9aa8-57e9-a751-379ed8038581"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-31543bec-7415-5c0a-b5bd-5fe9b03eaa24" :answer/id #uuid "31543bec-7415-5c0a-b5bd-5fe9b03eaa24" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "sup(A)=-\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}\\in A" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-fc17b842-d919-52cc-a3ae-905dd3045738" :answer/id #uuid "fc17b842-d919-52cc-a3ae-905dd3045738" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "sup(A)=-\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}\\notin A" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-66c0e3c3-432e-504d-94dc-f89ea3bb6e76" :answer/id #uuid "66c0e3c3-432e-504d-94dc-f89ea3bb6e76" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "sup(A)=\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{3}}\\in A" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-7d275fd5-7007-526a-9ff9-feaa35579085" :answer/id #uuid "7d275fd5-7007-526a-9ff9-feaa35579085" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "sup(A)=\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{3}}\\notin A" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-df2b4c83-9aa8-57e9-a751-379ed8038581" :answer/id #uuid "df2b4c83-9aa8-57e9-a751-379ed8038581" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$sup(A)$ does not exist" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186068894 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-07e2ee89-2122-51d1-b017-410fc7074e1d" "question-2aed86e1-b290-5c0a-9731-7ce89e296450"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id 17592186068670 :question/problem "Calculate the slope of the line that passes through the points $(1, 5)$ and $(4, 2).$" :question/worked-solution "We let $(x_1,y_1) = (1,5)$ and $(x_2,y_2) = (4,2),$ and compute the slope using the formula:\n\n$$\n\\eqalign{\n\t\tm &= \\dfrac {y_2 - y_1} {x_2 - x_1} \\\n\t\t    &= \\dfrac {2 - 5} {4 - 1} \\\n\t\t    &= \\dfrac {-3}{3} \\\n\t\t    &= -1\n\t}\n$$\n\nThus, the slope is $m=-1.$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186068893 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-46266ffe-395d-5bff-927f-737b6f2fbdfc" "question-e43571cc-c5ba-5976-8130-23aea630ac69"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id 17592186068669 :question/worked-solution "Note that the line passes through the points $(-2,0)$ and $(0,2).$ So, we let $(x_1,y_1) = (-2,0)$ and $(x_2,y_2) = (0,2),$ and compute the slope using the formula:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}m & =\\frac{{y}_{2}-{y}_{1}}{{x}_{2}-{x}_{1}} \\\\  & =\\frac{2-0}{0-(-2)} \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{2} \\\\  & =1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the slope of the line is $m=1.$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186068781 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-2103cab0-1d81-5f91-a28f-571868b98f97" "question-a9a75d95-73e5-5e15-b9cb-e6db140f14c6"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id 17592186068623 :question/worked-solution "The slope of the vertical line is undefined. We can see this by choosing two points on the line, such as $(4,0)$ and $(4,1),$ and computing the slope between them:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}m=\\frac{{y}_{2}-{y}_{1}}{{x}_{2}-{x}_{1}}=\\frac{1-0}{4-4}=\\frac{1}{0}=\\text{undefined}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nOn the other hand, the slope of the horizontal line is zero. We can see this by choosing two points on the line, such as $(0,3)$ and $(1,3),$ and computing the slope between them:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}m=\\frac{{y}_{2}-{y}_{1}}{{x}_{2}-{x}_{1}}=\\frac{3-3}{1-0}=\\frac{0}{1}=0\\end{aligned}\n$$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186068895 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-9ded7e32-d6f0-5c00-a36c-5bd0cb7be591" "question-4ae450be-6c03-5808-a0a9-2f2259b5d227" "question-91f45dce-63dd-5f77-bbe4-902a00f07621" "question-b320544f-ffed-5ad0-8747-600ca9ce31f5"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "question-07e2ee89-2122-51d1-b017-410fc7074e1d" :question/id #uuid "07e2ee89-2122-51d1-b017-410fc7074e1d" :question/math-academy-id "q-44612" :question/problem "Calculate the slope of the line that passes through the points $(-2,-4)$ and $(-8,-6).$" :question/worked-solution "We let $({x}_{1},{y}_{1})=(-2,-4)$ and $({x}_{2},{y}_{2})=(-8,-6),$ and compute the slope using the formula:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\begin{aligned}m & =\\frac{{y}_{2}-{y}_{1}}{{x}_{2}-{x}_{1}} \\\\  & =\\frac{-6-(-4)}{-8-(-2)} \\\\  & =\\frac{-2}{-6} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThus, the slope is $m=\\frac{1}{3}.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-09a3abf4-2ea3-5b6b-beac-3b3760d7c5cc"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-09a3abf4-2ea3-5b6b-beac-3b3760d7c5cc" :answer-field/id #uuid "09a3abf4-2ea3-5b6b-beac-3b3760d7c5cc" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-fce35e1b-eeb8-5c7a-8c3c-c04d0f68ee8c" :answer-field/choices ["answer-ada2b6cc-8e62-59e3-9964-b9408db65b59" "answer-3d02e444-7565-5de9-a078-504b2191fcd0" "answer-fce35e1b-eeb8-5c7a-8c3c-c04d0f68ee8c" "answer-902f202c-a83c-5fd8-9fbf-f740c2241181" "answer-e9b48d10-0c79-5e16-b619-e90a392edcd7"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-ada2b6cc-8e62-59e3-9964-b9408db65b59" :answer/id #uuid "ada2b6cc-8e62-59e3-9964-b9408db65b59" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-3d02e444-7565-5de9-a078-504b2191fcd0" :answer/id #uuid "3d02e444-7565-5de9-a078-504b2191fcd0" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-fce35e1b-eeb8-5c7a-8c3c-c04d0f68ee8c" :answer/id #uuid "fce35e1b-eeb8-5c7a-8c3c-c04d0f68ee8c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{3}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-902f202c-a83c-5fd8-9fbf-f740c2241181" :answer/id #uuid "902f202c-a83c-5fd8-9fbf-f740c2241181" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{3}{4}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-e9b48d10-0c79-5e16-b619-e90a392edcd7" :answer/id #uuid "e9b48d10-0c79-5e16-b619-e90a392edcd7" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{4}{3}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-2aed86e1-b290-5c0a-9731-7ce89e296450" :question/id #uuid "2aed86e1-b290-5c0a-9731-7ce89e296450" :question/math-academy-id "q-12633" :question/problem "What is the slope of a line that passes through the points $(0,3)$ and $(5,6)?$" :question/worked-solution "We let $({x}_{1},{y}_{1})=(0,3)$ and $({x}_{2},{y}_{2})=(5,6),$ and compute the slope using the formula:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\begin{aligned}m & =\\frac{{y}_{2}-{y}_{1}}{{x}_{2}-{x}_{1}} \\\\  & =\\frac{6-3}{5-0} \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{5}\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThus, the slope is $m=\\frac{3}{5}.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-c81a4e80-6d0f-54c9-a9b1-a145d88b8558"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-c81a4e80-6d0f-54c9-a9b1-a145d88b8558" :answer-field/id #uuid "c81a4e80-6d0f-54c9-a9b1-a145d88b8558" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-59c3c247-bf87-5cc9-927f-fae854845a54" :answer-field/choices ["answer-996c1ad0-79b6-5ad6-bb02-d19eb924c5e9" "answer-d7ba74f0-8e9a-56c5-83d1-49d861acc4a4" "answer-3eda3d1b-be86-5d59-ba68-d86735eb257a" "answer-59c3c247-bf87-5cc9-927f-fae854845a54" "answer-2f5b2164-de5d-580a-9044-b5a6ace56295"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-996c1ad0-79b6-5ad6-bb02-d19eb924c5e9" :answer/id #uuid "996c1ad0-79b6-5ad6-bb02-d19eb924c5e9" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "3" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-d7ba74f0-8e9a-56c5-83d1-49d861acc4a4" :answer/id #uuid "d7ba74f0-8e9a-56c5-83d1-49d861acc4a4" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "5" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-3eda3d1b-be86-5d59-ba68-d86735eb257a" :answer/id #uuid "3eda3d1b-be86-5d59-ba68-d86735eb257a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{5}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-59c3c247-bf87-5cc9-927f-fae854845a54" :answer/id #uuid "59c3c247-bf87-5cc9-927f-fae854845a54" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{3}{5}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-2f5b2164-de5d-580a-9044-b5a6ace56295" :answer/id #uuid "2f5b2164-de5d-580a-9044-b5a6ace56295" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{5}{3}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-46266ffe-395d-5bff-927f-737b6f2fbdfc" :question/id #uuid "46266ffe-395d-5bff-927f-737b6f2fbdfc" :question/math-academy-id "q-26714" :question/problem "![](images/10/10f79e3e129891e51ee47ecd595ab666053cd048688c4a63e8f7edd66cdae6da.png)\n\nGiven that the line above passes through the point $(-4,-1)$ and intersects the $x$-axis when $x=4,$ find the slope of the line." :question/worked-solution "Note that the line passes through the points $(-4,-1)$ and $(4,0).$ So, we let $({x}_{1},{y}_{1})=(-4,-1)$ and $({x}_{2},{y}_{2})=(4,0),$ and compute the slope using the formula:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}m & =\\frac{{y}_{2}-{y}_{1}}{{x}_{2}-{x}_{1}} \\\\  & =\\frac{0-(-1)}{4-(-4)} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{8}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the slope of the line is $m=\\frac{1}{8}.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-61012383-9b90-523d-b36d-7d0e995b871e"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-61012383-9b90-523d-b36d-7d0e995b871e" :answer-field/id #uuid "61012383-9b90-523d-b36d-7d0e995b871e" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-8f66d13c-71b8-57c5-923e-237f1dcc96ee" :answer-field/choices ["answer-4f3bc186-d96f-5413-afa5-401d93963056" "answer-f2e31773-4151-5e13-b6f5-e20c2e64929c" "answer-8f66d13c-71b8-57c5-923e-237f1dcc96ee" "answer-c534aa13-e3d3-5556-960f-588b6885f1a1" "answer-104d41c3-0e85-52e1-9ce5-444595605652"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-4f3bc186-d96f-5413-afa5-401d93963056" :answer/id #uuid "4f3bc186-d96f-5413-afa5-401d93963056" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-f2e31773-4151-5e13-b6f5-e20c2e64929c" :answer/id #uuid "f2e31773-4151-5e13-b6f5-e20c2e64929c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{4}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-8f66d13c-71b8-57c5-923e-237f1dcc96ee" :answer/id #uuid "8f66d13c-71b8-57c5-923e-237f1dcc96ee" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{8}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-c534aa13-e3d3-5556-960f-588b6885f1a1" :answer/id #uuid "c534aa13-e3d3-5556-960f-588b6885f1a1" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{3}{8}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-104d41c3-0e85-52e1-9ce5-444595605652" :answer/id #uuid "104d41c3-0e85-52e1-9ce5-444595605652" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{5}{4}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-e43571cc-c5ba-5976-8130-23aea630ac69" :question/id #uuid "e43571cc-c5ba-5976-8130-23aea630ac69" :question/math-academy-id "q-26606" :question/problem "![](images/64/64957c4f5315d4880503aa6572699a675b4c16143ae08e58fb25df37fd69d05d.png)\n\nThe straight line shown above intersects the $y$-axis when $y=3$ and intersects the $x$-axis when $x=-6.$ What is its slope?" :question/worked-solution "Note that the line passes through the points $(0,3)$ and $(-6,0).$ So, we let $({x}_{1},{y}_{1})=(0,3)$ and $({x}_{2},{y}_{2})=(-6,0),$ and compute the slope using the formula:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}m & =\\frac{{y}_{2}-{y}_{1}}{{x}_{2}-{x}_{1}} \\\\  & =\\frac{0-3}{-6-0} \\\\  & =\\frac{-3}{-6} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the slope of the line is $m=\\frac{1}{2}.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-f998fecd-bbe8-5d5d-9d3d-12e2694181ea"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-f998fecd-bbe8-5d5d-9d3d-12e2694181ea" :answer-field/id #uuid "f998fecd-bbe8-5d5d-9d3d-12e2694181ea" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-0caedf90-341d-52e8-a42d-3d261ab0113f" :answer-field/choices ["answer-ffff2fe5-2627-5cc8-a2de-2858384dd99a" "answer-0caedf90-341d-52e8-a42d-3d261ab0113f" "answer-8fb6c2a4-f6d5-5d7d-a84f-6d0459626d22" "answer-063cb6bd-a8a2-5aa5-95be-42d1d654b497" "answer-6b76e92b-c74d-56a1-a29f-b50300fd87eb"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-ffff2fe5-2627-5cc8-a2de-2858384dd99a" :answer/id #uuid "ffff2fe5-2627-5cc8-a2de-2858384dd99a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-0caedf90-341d-52e8-a42d-3d261ab0113f" :answer/id #uu