f papers, $\\frac{3}{8},$ as follows:\n\n$$\n3÷\\frac{3}{8}\n$$\n\nTo divide by a fraction, we multiply by the fraction's reciprocal:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3÷\\frac{3}{8} & =3\\times \\frac{8}{3} \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{1}\\times \\frac{8}{3} \\\\  & =\\frac{3\\times 8}{1\\times 3} \\\\  & =\\frac{24}{3} \\\\  & =24÷3 \\\\  & =8\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the unit rate is $8$ hours per paper. To find the number of hours that Marcel takes to transcribe $5$ papers, we multiply the unit rate by $5$ papers and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}8\\times 5 & =40.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, Marcel can transcribe $5$ papers in $40$ hours." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-9e93abd1-2bd1-5379-bc1e-5642481b5dbb"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-9e93abd1-2bd1-5379-bc1e-5642481b5dbb" :answer-field/id #uuid "9e93abd1-2bd1-5379-bc1e-5642481b5dbb" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-0310f6ae-86ed-5bcd-8506-b6e65fb54b2e" :answer-field/choices ["answer-9b90d420-15e0-51d3-9e07-c2cac59126f1" "answer-8110aae0-922c-5223-9c2a-82d6828da2ad" "answer-fb0c21ff-4f96-5117-8019-31abfd00c5c4" "answer-0310f6ae-86ed-5bcd-8506-b6e65fb54b2e" "answer-898375ff-a273-5654-b1a5-b4ae553658aa"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-9b90d420-15e0-51d3-9e07-c2cac59126f1" :answer/id #uuid "9b90d420-15e0-51d3-9e07-c2cac59126f1" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$20$ hours" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-8110aae0-922c-5223-9c2a-82d6828da2ad" :answer/id #uuid "8110aae0-922c-5223-9c2a-82d6828da2ad" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$25$ hours" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-fb0c21ff-4f96-5117-8019-31abfd00c5c4" :answer/id #uuid "fb0c21ff-4f96-5117-8019-31abfd00c5c4" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$32$ hours" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-0310f6ae-86ed-5bcd-8506-b6e65fb54b2e" :answer/id #uuid "0310f6ae-86ed-5bcd-8506-b6e65fb54b2e" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$40$ hours" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-898375ff-a273-5654-b1a5-b4ae553658aa" :answer/id #uuid "898375ff-a273-5654-b1a5-b4ae553658aa" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$8$ hours" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-6ee32ba5-d533-567a-a32c-16aed9424364" :question/id #uuid "6ee32ba5-d533-567a-a32c-16aed9424364" :question/math-academy-id "q-148226" :question/problem "Laura can decorate $5$ cakes in $\\frac{5}{2}$ hours. How many cakes can she decorate in $3$ hours?" :question/worked-solution "To determine the number of cakes Laura can decorate in $3$ hours, we first find the unit rate of cakes per hour and then multiply it by $3$ hours.\n\nTo find the unit rate of cakes per hour, we divide the number of cakes, $5,$ by the number of hours, $\\frac{5}{2},$ as follows:\n\n$$\n5÷\\frac{5}{2}\n$$\n\nTo divide by a fraction, we multiply by the fraction's reciprocal:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}5÷\\frac{5}{2} & =5\\times \\frac{2}{5} \\\\  & =\\frac{5}{1}\\times \\frac{2}{5} \\\\  & =\\frac{5\\times 2}{1\\times 5} \\\\  & =\\frac{10}{5} \\\\  & =10÷5 \\\\  & =2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the unit rate is $2$ cakes per hour. To determine the number of cakes Laura can decorate in $3$ hours, we multiply the unit rate by $3$ hours and get\n\n$$\n2\\times 3=6.\n$$\n\nTherefore, Laura can decorate $6$ cakes in $3$ hours." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-f90489e0-fda9-52b4-aa57-bb15b814888a"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-f90489e0-fda9-52b4-aa57-bb15b814888a" :answer-field/id #uuid "f90489e0-fda9-52b4-aa57-bb15b814888a" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-52d29a71-945d-530d-a118-ccf4c6730562" :answer-field/choices ["answer-b446b045-dc82-596f-8d46-675e569a086b" "answer-8085cb4b-293b-5f54-931d-315952